## Part 4: Using GitHub's Web Interface Efficiently

### Quick Method: Upload Multiple Files

Instead of creating files one by one, you can:

1. **Create all files locally on your computer** first
2. Go to your GitHub repository
3. Click **"Add file"** → **"Upload files"**
4. Drag and drop entire folders (GitHub maintains structure)
5. Commit the changes

### Even Faster: Use GitHub Desktop (Optional)

1. Download **GitHub Desktop** (desktop.github.com)
2. Clone your repository to your computer
3. Create all files/folders locally using your file explorer
4. Open GitHub Desktop, it will detect changes
5. Commit and push to GitHub

